feature.file:
@AVAILABLE_CREDIT @SPEND_BALANCE_ALERTS Feature: Spend Balance API - Available Credit Event
@AC01 @SUCCESS @SANITY @REGRESSION @LAYER6 Scenario Outline: AC01 - Successfully process a availablecredit event and send email Given a valid client "aeoutfitters" with an active account of type "<accountType>" from channel "alerts-ui" With <emailEnrolled> and <textEnrolled> And the customer language is "<language>" And the availableCredit event has current available credit "<current>" with credit limit "<limit>" When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 202 And the response should contain the message "Event accepted for processing" And the response should include a non-empty "eventId" matching the CloudEvent id And the response should include the "X-SYF-TransactionId" header And an outbound event should be published with status "CONSUMED" followed by "PROCESSED" And the outbound delivery status should be "SUCCESS" with reason code "SUCCESS_DELIVERED"
Examples: | accountType | language | current | limit | emailEnrolled | textEnrolled | | PLCC | en | 850.00 | 2000.00 | true | true | | PLCC | es | 850.00 | 1000.05 | true | false | | PLCC | en | 600.00 | 2500.00 | false | true | | PLCC | es | 1500.00 | 5000.20 | true | true | | DUALCARD | en | 2500.00 | 30500.00 | true | false | | DUALCARD | en | 700.00 | 1500.00 | true | true |
@AC02 @SUCCESS @SANITY @REGRESSION @LAYER6 Scenario Outline: AC02 - American Eagle cardholder at the collections boundary (pastDueAmount = <pastDueAmount>) still receives the available-credit email Given a valid client "aeoutfitters" with an active account of type "<accountType>" from channel "alerts-ui" With <emailEnrolled> and <textEnrolled> And the customer language is "<language>" And the account has a past due amount of "<pastDueAmount>" When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 202 And an outbound event should be published with status "CONSUMED" followed by "PROCESSED" And the outbound delivery status should be "SUCCESS" with reason code "SUCCESS_DELIVERED"
Examples: | pastDueAmount | accountType | language | emailEnrolled | textEnrolled | | 0.00 | PLCC | en | true | true | | 1.00 | DUALCARD | es | true | true |
@AC03 @SUPPRESSION @REGRESSION @LAYER6 Scenario: AC03 - Available-credit email is suppressed for a delinquent American Eagle cardholder account Given a delinquent account at index 0 from test data for client "aeoutfitters" of type "PLCC" from channel "alerts-ui" When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 202 And an outbound event should be published with status "CONSUMED" followed by "SUPPRESSED" And the outbound reason code should be "SUPPRESS_COLL_DELINQUENT" And the outbound reason description should be "Suppressed due to delinquent days exceeding threshold: {delinquentDays}"
@AC04 @SUPPRESSION @REGRESSION @LAYER6 Scenario Outline: AC04 - Available-credit email is suppressed for American Eagle cardholder account with blocked external status "<externalStatus>" Given a valid client "aeoutfitters" with an account of type "<cardType>" from channel "alerts-ui" and external status "<externalStatus>" When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 202 And an outbound event should be published with status "CONSUMED" followed by "SUPPRESSED" And the outbound reason code should be "SUPPRESS_ACCT_STATUS" And the outbound reason description should be "Account suppressed due to blocked external status: <externalStatus>"
# Note: External status Z has all errors on updating in TDMP - kept commented out in examples Examples: | externalStatus | cardType| | B | PLCC | | L | PLCC | | U | DUALCARD| # | Z | DUALCARD| | I | DUALCARD|
@AC05 @SUPPRESSION @REGRESSION @LAYER6 Scenario Outline: AC05 - Available-credit email is suppressed for American Eagle cardholder account with blocked misc code "<miscCode>" Given a valid client "aeoutfitters" with an account of type "<cardType>" from channel "alerts-ui" and misc code "<miscCode>" When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 202 And an outbound event should be published with status "CONSUMED" followed by "SUPPRESSED" And the outbound reason code should be "SUPPRESS_ACCT_MISC_CODE" And the outbound reason description should be "Account suppressed due to blocked misc code: <miscCode>"
Examples: | miscCode | cardType| | NBA | PLCC | | NBK | PLCC | | MBA | DUALCARD| | MBK | PLCC | | MDK | PLCC | | ZER | DUALCARD| | MBS | DUALCARD| | H01 | DUALCARD| | H02 | PLCC | | H03 | PLCC | | H04 | PLCC | | H05 | PLCC | | H11 | PLCC | | H12 | DUALCARD| | HRR | DUALCARD| | HZR | DUALCARD| | Y01 | PLCC | | Y08 | PLCC | | YDB | PLCC | | YE1 | PLCC | | YE2 | DUALCARD| | YE3 | DUALCARD| | YE4 | DUALCARD| | XCX | DUALCARD| | YSY | DUALCARD|
@AC06a @BAD_REQUEST @REGRESSION @NEGATIVE Scenario Outline: AC06a - Available-credit event is rejected when required field "<field>" is missing from the request Given the availableCredit request has the field "<field>" removed from the payload When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 400 And the response message should be "Validation failed" And the response errors array should contain field "cloudEvent" with message "<errorMessage>" And no outbound event should be published
Examples: Envelope - mandatory CloudEvent attributes (L1) | field | errorMessage | | cloudEvent.id | Missing mandatory id attribute | | cloudEvent.source | Missing mandatory source attribute | | cloudEvent.type | Missing mandatory type attribute | | cloudEvent.specversion | Missing mandatory specversion attribute |
@AC06b @BAD_REQUEST @REGRESSION @NEGATIVE Scenario Outline: AC06a - Available-credit event is rejected when required field "<field>" is missing from the request Given the availableCredit request has the field "<field>" removed from the payload When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 400 And the response message should be "Validation failed" And the response errors array should contain field "<field>" with message "<errorMessage>" And no outbound event should be published
Examples: Envelope - mandatory CloudEvent attributes (L1) | field | errorMessage | | cloudEvent.data | CloudEvent.data is required |
Examples: eventHeader - mandatory business fields (L4) | field | errorMessage | | data.eventHeader | eventHeader is required | | data.eventHeader.eventType | eventType is required | | data.eventHeader.channel | channel is required | | data.eventHeader.timestamp | timestamp is required | | data.eventHeader.transId | transId is required | | data.eventHeader.version | version is required | | data.eventHeader.fiToken | fiToken is required |
Examples: delivery - mandatory routing fields (L4) | field | errorMessage | | data.delivery | delivery is required | | data.delivery.identifier | delivery identifier is required |
Examples: analytics - mandatory tracking fields (L4) | field | errorMessage | | data.analytics | analytics is required | | data.analytics.uuid | uuid is required |
# Note: creditLimit field errors below are [TBD-PRD] - replace with verbatim text from PRD Â§4.3 Examples: creditLimit - mandatory balance fields (L4) | field | errorMessage | | data.creditLimit | creditLimit is required | | data.creditLimit.creditLimitThresholdField | creditLimitThresholdField is required | | data.creditLimit.openToBuyAmount | openToBuyAmount is required |
@AC06c @BAD_REQUEST @REGRESSION @NEGATIVE Scenario: AC06b - Available-credit event is rejected when "cloudEvent.specversion" contains invalid value "2.0" Given the availableCredit request has the field "cloudEvent.specversion" set to invalid value "2.0" When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 400 And the response message should be "Validation failed" And the response errors array should contain field "cloudEvent" with message "Invalid specversion: 2.0" And no outbound event should be published
@AC06d @BAD_REQUEST @REGRESSION @NEGATIVE Scenario Outline: AC06c - Available-credit event is rejected when "<field>" contains invalid value "<value>" Given the availableCredit request has the field "<field>" set to invalid value "<value>" When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 400 And the response message should be "Validation failed" And the response errors array should contain field "<field>" with message "<errorMessage>" And no outbound event should be published
Examples: Envelope - invalid CloudEvent attribute values (L1) | field | value | errorMessage | | cloudEvent.source | urn:syf:UNKNOWN_SOURCE | CloudEvent.source is not on the allow-list | | cloudEvent.type | not.a.valid.type | CloudEvent.type does not match the configured pattern | | cloudEvent.type | com.syf.alerts.unknown.v1 | CloudEvent.type is not on the allow-list |
Examples: eventHeader - invalid business field values (L4) | field | value | errorMessage | | data.eventHeader.version | 99.0 |Unsupported version: 99.0 for event type: availableCredit |
# Note: creditLimit invalid-value errors below are [TBD-PRD] Examples: creditLimit - invalid balance values (L4) | field | value | errorMessage | | data.creditLimit.creditLimitThresholdField | abc | creditLimitThresholdField must be a valid numeric amount (e.g., 500.00) | | data.creditLimit.openToBuyAmount | xyz | openToBuyAmount must be a valid numeric amount (e.g., 1200.50) |
Examples: Cross-field consistency - mismatched envelope vs payload values (L5) | field | value | errorMessage | | data.analytics.uuid | 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111 | data.analytics.uuid does not match cloudEvent.id | | data.eventHeader.eventType | balanceThreshold | Unsupported event type: balanceThreshold | | data.eventHeader.version | 2.0 | Unsupported version: 2.0 for event type: availableCredit |
@AC06e @BAD_REQUEST @REGRESSION @NEGATIVE Scenario Outline: AC06d - Available-credit event is rejected when required field "<field>" is blank Given the availableCredit request has the field "<field>" set to a blank value When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 400 And the response message should be "Validation failed" And the response errors array should contain field "<field>" with message "<errorMessage>" And no outbound event should be published
Examples: eventHeader - blank business fields | field | errorMessage | | data.eventHeader.eventType | eventType is required | | data.eventHeader.channel | channel is required | | data.eventHeader.timestamp | timestamp is required | | data.eventHeader.transId | transId is required | | data.eventHeader.version | version is required | | data.eventHeader.fiToken | fiToken is required |
Examples: delivery - blank routing fields | field | errorMessage | | data.delivery.identifier | delivery identifier is required |
Examples: creditLimit - blank balance fields | field | errorMessage | | data.creditLimit.creditLimitThresholdField | creditLimitThresholdField must be a valid numeric amount (e.g., 500.00) | | data.creditLimit.openToBuyAmount | openToBuyAmount must be a valid numeric amount (e.g., 1200.50) |
Examples: analytics - blank tracking fields | field | errorMessage | | data.analytics.uuid | data.analytics.uuid does not match cloudEvent.id |
@AC06f @BAD_REQUEST @REGRESSION @NEGATIVE @LAYER3 Scenario: AC06e - Available-credit event is rejected when the data payload cannot be deserialized Given the availableCredit request has a malformed "data" payload that cannot be deserialized When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 400 And the response message should be "Validation failed" And the response errors array should contain field "cloudEvent" with a message starting with "Unexpected character ('}' (code 125)): was expecting double-quote to start field name" And no outbound event should be published
@AC06g @BAD_REQUEST @REGRESSION @NEGATIVE @LAYER3 Scenario: AC06f - Available-credit event is rejected when the HTTP body is unparseable Given the availableCredit request has an unparseable HTTP body When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 400 And the response message should be "Validation failed" And the response errors array should contain field "cloudEvent" with message "Unexpected end-of-input within/between Object entries" And no outbound event should be published
@AC06h @BAD_REQUEST @REGRESSION @NEGATIVE @LAYER2 Scenario Outline: AC06g - Available-credit event is rejected when Content-Type is "<contentType>" instead of application/cloudevents+json Given a static valid availableCredit payload is prepared And the request Content-Type is overridden to "<contentType>" When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 415 And the response message should be "Must be application/cloudevents+json" And the response errors array should contain field "Header.Content-Type" with message "Unsupported media type: <contentType><message>" And no outbound event should be published
Examples: | contentType | message | | application/json | | | text/plain |;charset=ISO-8859-1 | | text/xml |;charset=ISO-8859-1 |
@AC07 @SERVER_ERROR @REGRESSION @NEGATIVE @LAYER7 Scenario: AC07 - An unexpected system fault returns HTTP 500 with no outbound event or notification Given a fault-triggering account for client "american eagle" from channel "alerts-ui" When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 500 And the response message should be "Internal server error" And no outbound event should be published
@AC08 @SUPPRESSION @REGRESSION @LAYER6 Scenario: AC08 - Available-credit email is suppressed for a delinquent American Eagle cardholder account Given a delinquent account at index 1 from test data for client "aeoutfitters" of type "DAULCARD" from channel "alerts-ui" When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API Then the API should respond with HTTP status 202 And an outbound event should be published with status "CONSUMED" followed by "SUPPRESSED" And the outbound reason code should be "SUPPRESS_COLL_DELINQUENT" And the outbound reason description should be "Suppressed due to delinquent days exceeding threshold: {delinquentDays}"
### Below Scenarios validation can't achieve throught the test automation ####
## Scenario can't be automated as it requires to create a test account with past due amount and due date within 1 day. This is not possible to create through automation as it requires to wait for the due date to be within 1 day. ###
