### Below Scenarios validation can't achieve throught the test automation #### #@AC12 @INTEGRATION_ERROR @REGRESSION @LAYER6 #Scenario: AC11 - Available-credit event produces CONSUMED then FAILED when account metadata integration cannot be reached # Spec Â§7.2.2.3: INTG_ERROR_ACCT_METADATA - terminal FAILED state with no delivery # Requires a test account whose metadata cannot be fetched by AccountMetadataProvider #Given an account that triggers "ACCT_METADATA" integration failure for client "aeoutfitters" from channel "alerts-ui" #When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API #Then the API should respond with HTTP status 202 #And an outbound event should be published with status "CONSUMED" followed by "FAILED" #And the outbound reason code should be "INTG_ERROR_ACCT_METADATA" # And the outbound reason description should be "Account metadata integration failure"
#@AC13 @INTEGRATION_ERROR @REGRESSION @LAYER6 #Scenario: AC13 - Available-credit event produces CONSUMED then FAILED when account summary integration cannot be reached # Spec Â§7.2.2.3: INTG_ERROR_ACCT_SUMMARY - terminal FAILED state with no delivery # Requires a test account whose summary cannot be fetched by AccountSummaryProvider #Given an account that triggers "ACCT_SUMMARY" integration failure for client "aeoutfitters" from channel "alerts-ui" #When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API #Then the API should respond with HTTP status 202 #And an outbound event should be published with status "CONSUMED" followed by "FAILED" #And the outbound reason code should be "INTG_ERROR_ACCT_SUMMARY" #And the outbound reason description should be "Account summary integration failure"
#@AC14 @INTEGRATION_ERROR @REGRESSION @LAYER6 #Scenario: AC14 - Available-credit event produces CONSUMED then PROCESSED with delivery FAILED when email delivery integration fails # Spec Â§7.2.2.3: INTG_ERROR_DLVR_EMAIL - PROCESSED with delivery.status = FAILED # Requires a test account whose email delivery is configured to fail in the Zeta ESP V2 test environment #Given an account that triggers "DLVR_EMAIL" integration failure for client "aeoutfitters" from channel "alerts-ui" #When the availableCredit event is submitted to the Alerts Spend Balance API #Then the API should respond with HTTP status 202 #And an outbound event should be published with status "CONSUMED" followed by "PROCESSED" #And the outbound delivery status should be "FAILED" with reason code "INTG_ERROR_DLVR_EMAIL" #And the outbound delivery reason description should be "Email delivery integration failure"
